      "values:originalText": "Repeal the subsection, substitute:\n\n(1) A person holding office as Chief Minister vacates the office:\n\n(a) when the person resigns the office; or\n\n(b) when the person ceases to be a member (not because of a\ngeneral election); or\n\n(c) immediately before a Chief Minister is elected after:\n\n(i) the next general election; or\n\n(ii) the passing of a resolution of no confidence in the Chief\nMinister.\n\n(1A) A person holding office as a Minister (other than the Chief\nMinister) vacates the office:\n\n(a) when the person resigns the office; or\n\n(b) when the person ceases to be a member (not because of a\ngeneral election); or\n\n(c) when the person is dismissed from office by the Chief\nMinister; or\n\n(d) immediately before another Chief Minister is elected after:\n\n(i) the next general election; or\n\nSchedule 1  Australian Capital Territory (Self-Government) Act 1988\n\n(ii) the passing of a resolution of no confidence in the Chief\nMinister.",
