      "dc:source": "australian-capital-territory-legislation-amendment-act-2003.pdf, p.9",
      "values:originalText": "Insert:\n\n(6A) If the full-time member is precluded from being present by\nsection 42, then:\n\n(a) if the full-time member is the Chairperson—any 3 members\nconstitute a quorum; or\n\n(b) if the full-time member is not the Chairperson—the\nChairperson and any other 2 members constitute a quorum.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 28 August 2002\nSenate on 19 September 2002]\n\n(178/02)",
      "skos:definition": "Insert:\n\n(6A) If the full-time member is precluded from being present by\nsection 42, then:\n\n(a) if the full-time member is the Chairperson—any 3 members\nconstitute a quorum; or\n\n(b) if the full-time member is not the Chairperson—the\nChairperson and any other 2 members constitute a quorum.\n\n[Minister’s second reading speech made in—\nHouse of Representatives on 28 August 2002\nSenate on 19 September 2002]\n\n(178/02)",
